16:56.129 --> 16:58.506
<i>Since the first victim
at Quahog Park last week,</i>

16:58.632 --> 17:02.260
<i>three more men have been killed,
all of them very, very fat.</i>

17:02.511 --> 17:05.972
- Lois, that sketch looks a lot like Patrick.
- Oh, that's ridiculous.

17:06.055 --> 17:09.601
I don't know. I mean, he's clearly crazy.
Look at that imaginary wife of his.

17:09.684 --> 17:13.145
Well, if she's imaginary, how do you
explain the pickle on the couch?

17:13.228 --> 17:17.273
I don't understand what...
Oh, wait. What? Really?

17:17.774 --> 17:20.317
- Hey, Stewie!
- I know, I know. I heard!

17:22.821 --> 17:24.196
Patrick.

17:24.738 --> 17:25.948
Where have you been?

17:26.448 --> 17:29.285
Oh, it's nothing you need
to concern yourself with, Lois.

17:29.369 --> 17:30.953
Well, that's a relief.

17:31.078 --> 17:32.496
Oh, yeah. Yeah, that's a relief.

17:32.580 --> 17:36.124
Yeah, the Fat Guy Strangler's living here
and there's a fat guy in the house.

17:36.208 --> 17:39.628
This'll be a bigger disaster than
when Peter did Tara Reid's boob job.

17:41.463 --> 17:43.172
Dropped some pepperoni on there.

17:43.548 --> 17:44.841
You know what? That works. Sew it up.

17:47.009 --> 17:48.970
Michael was one of our brothers.

17:49.054 --> 17:51.848
He was a good man. He was a kind man.

17:52.515 --> 17:55.143
- He was a fat man.
- And now he's a dead man.

17:55.267 --> 17:58.520
And we're all next.
The Fat Guy Strangler's gonna get us.

17:58.646 --> 17:59.688
- He's right.
- Oh, my God.

17:59.813 --> 18:01.148
- We're finished.
- Will someone tie my shoe?

18:01.273 --> 18:03.608
People, people!
I know what will make us feel better.

18:03.692 --> 18:06.695
Let us sing the NAAFP anthem.

19:15.177 --> 19:17.094
All right, everybody,
just make yourselves at home.

19:17.220 --> 19:19.555
Lois, these are the fat guys. Fat guys, Lois.

19:19.638 --> 19:21.725
My God, look at you fat bastards.

19:21.807 --> 19:24.059
I bet none of you can even find
your own penis.

19:24.184 --> 19:26.728
Find your penis for a dollar.
Find your penis, one dollar.

19:26.853 --> 19:29.064
One dollar, find your penis.
Find your penis here.

19:29.147 --> 19:30.607
Peter, what's going on?

19:30.691 --> 19:32.358
Lois, my people are in danger.

19:32.442 --> 19:35.194
Until they find the Fat Guy Strangler,
we will stay...

19:35.278 --> 19:36.445
Victor, don't lean against that.

19:37.654 --> 19:38.740
Hey, everybody.

19:38.823 --> 19:40.574
Peter, you gotta get
these guys out of here.

19:40.658 --> 19:42.534
- Patrick is the murderer.
- What?

19:43.368 --> 19:44.995
You son of a bitch!

19:45.121 --> 19:48.081
Don't listen to Brian.
He doesn't know what he's talking about.

19:48.165 --> 19:50.417
Out of my way, Lois. Your brother is toast.

19:50.500 --> 19:52.252
Warm buttery toast!

19:53.628 --> 19:55.421
- That sounds good.
- I love toast.

19:55.505 --> 19:58.007
- I just found my penis.
- Run, Patrick, run!

19:58.133 --> 19:59.425
After him!

20:01.386 --> 20:03.054
Boys, to your Rascals!

20:10.728 --> 20:13.063
He went into James Woods.
Let's spread out and find him.

20:13.147 --> 20:14.649
We'll head him off at the...

20:16.484 --> 20:18.069
Todd, man, you got to chew your food.

20:20.321 --> 20:23.616
Brian, I know my brother.
He couldn't have done these things.

20:23.698 --> 20:26.284
Well, let's see if you feel that way
when you see this.

20:27.702 --> 20:28.786
Look.

20:34.751 --> 20:37.670
So he has pictures of himself
strangling fat guys.

20:37.796 --> 20:40.006
That doesn't mean
he's the Fat Guy Strangler.

20:40.130 --> 20:42.299
Oh, yeah? What about
the dead fat guy under his bed?

20:42.423 --> 20:43.508
Coincidence?

20:43.633 --> 20:45.718
What about the half-dead fat guy
in the corner?

20:45.843 --> 20:46.803
Patrick tried to kill me.

20:46.928 --> 20:49.471
- Well, maybe it's a different Patrick.
- Lois!

20:49.555 --> 20:52.058
Okay, okay. Oh, my God!

20:52.182 --> 20:54.102
- Peter's out there with him!
- Wait!

20:54.519 --> 20:55.979
You gonna eat that dead fat guy?

20:58.064 --> 20:59.732
How are we gonna find them?

20:59.856 --> 21:01.483
Don't worry, Lois.
I'm good at finding people.

21:01.609 --> 21:03.986
I was the one who found Bush
after Hurricane Katrina.

21:06.029 --> 21:08.614
- Mr. President, are you up there?
- Go away!

21:08.698 --> 21:11.785
<i>- Sir, there's a disaster in New Orleans.
- I'm reading Superfudge.</i>

21:11.868 --> 21:14.162
- You got to come down and deal with this.
- Don't make me do stuff.

21:15.455 --> 21:17.958
Patrick? Patrick!

21:18.333 --> 21:20.085
Crap! Guess we lost him.

21:20.209 --> 21:23.171
Well, nothing left to do
but finish this sentence uninterrupt...

21:26.757 --> 21:29.886
- Patrick, let him go!
- Don't come any closer!

21:30.010 --> 21:33.973
Patrick, let him go or Marian gets it.

21:34.098 --> 21:36.851
Nice try. But Marian's over there.

21:38.435 --> 21:40.229
Don't hurt her!

21:41.813 --> 21:44.316
- Now, let him go!
- Okay! Okay!

21:45.651 --> 21:47.194
- You missed!
- No, I didn't.

21:47.319 --> 21:50.863
That's for rolling up the damn window
when I tried to jump into the General Lee.

21:51.404 --> 21:54.824
I'm sorry, Lois.
I never meant to hurt anybody.

21:55.409 --> 21:59.078
I mean, I did mean to kill those fat guys,
but I never meant to hurt you.

21:59.204 --> 22:02.165
You may be very sick, Patrick,
but I love you.

22:02.331 --> 22:05.126
You're my brother
and you'll always be my brother.

22:05.251 --> 22:07.713
I have to go back to the hospital, don't I?

22:07.836 --> 22:09.423
Yeah. I'm afraid so.

22:09.547 --> 22:11.924
Hey, Patrick. Did you see
how that rock hit me in the face?

22:12.050 --> 22:13.885
It was like, pow, right in the kisser!

22:14.010 --> 22:15.177
Pow, right in the kisser!

22:15.303 --> 22:16.262
Pow, right in the kisser!

22:17.430 --> 22:19.974
Stop screaming, you can't hear me.
Pow, right in the kisser!

22:20.099 --> 22:21.141
Pow, right in the kisser!

22:21.267 --> 22:22.268
Pow, right in the kisser!

22:24.978 --> 22:26.230
I miss Uncle Patrick.

22:26.314 --> 22:29.483
Don't worry, kids.
I promise we can visit him once a month.

22:29.609 --> 22:31.318
We'll be his period.

22:32.027 --> 22:36.865
I was just upstairs and there's
a half-dead fat guy eating a dead fat guy.

22:39.284 --> 22:41.285
So I guess we're just looking
the other way, huh?

22:41.286 --> 23:42.286
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru